Week 1: Filling content

This week we explored how games are made up of different elements. The 3 elements we explored the most were:
Mechanics
Dynamics
Aesthetics

Each of these elements fundamentally impact how the game is played, and ultimately how this experience feels to the player. An example is a mechanic - a small action that the user can take: for example, pressing a button to make a player crouch. This action on its own doesn't make for much of a game, but if it is paired with another mechanic or rule (for instance: enemies can't see you when you are crouched behind something), the player is now incentivised to use this action. This can be called a dynamic.

